From 2e57aadffa5c9793fbbcdfd7c0e31fa6d910994b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 15:47:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Paper Trading Foundation (Milestone 5.1)

Introduces provider-abstracted paper trading on top of the existing
Signal Engine, without changing its logic or the existing /signal
API contract.

- OptionDataService interface (app/market/option_chain.py) with a
  Zerodha Kite Connect implementation (zerodha_option_data_service.py)
  as the only file that imports kiteconnect.
- paper_trade_service.py: SQLite-backed CRUD/persistence only
  (paper_trades, trade_events, trade_state tables).
- paper_trade_orchestrator.py: decides when trades open, are
  monitored, and close, using the Signal Engine's own entry/
  stop_loss/target1 values - no percentage-based rules.
- telegram.py: lifecycle notifications (signal generated, trade
  opened/closed, milestones, daily summary, system errors).
- New read-only endpoints: /paper-trades/open, /paper-trades/closed,
  /paper-trades/summary.
- Minimal fix to a pre-existing indentation/syntax bug in api.py so
  the app can actually start; no other changes to that file's
  existing behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
